On-device AI means that the smart things you use, like your phone, smart glasses, or a robot, use their own computer power to do AI tasks, instead of sending data to the internet or a server. Imagine if you had a calculator that could solve problems on your phone, not through a computer on the internet. On-device AI helps keep your data private and makes things faster, like recognizing faces in real time without needing a server to process everything.

